{"thought":"Now, I will create the new test file `tests/test_reprobot_tomlkit__440.py` with the test case that reproduces the issue. The test will load a TOML string with an inline table, add a new key, and then check the output of `dumps` to ensure that there is a newline before the new key. I will write the test and then run it to see if it fails as expected.","final_test":"import tomlkit


def test_missing_newline_after_inline_table():
    v = tomlkit.loads("""[x]\na.b = {}""")
    v["x"]["c"] = 3
    output = tomlkit.dumps(v)
    assert output == """[x]\na.b = {}\nc = 3"""  # Expecting a newline before 'c = 3'"}
